  "id": "COMPOUND:32178 - PROTEIN:4886",
  "verbalization": "Cryptobeilic Acid B is implicated in the activation of Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Cryptobeilic Acid B acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, (+)-Conocarpan, and (R,2E,4E)-7-(4-(Dimethylamino)Phenyl)-N,4,6-Trimethyl-7-Oxohepta-2,4-Dienamide, all of which are known to target the same kinase. This indicates a potential pathway where Cryptobeilic Acid B may influence the activity of Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR through the modulation of its downstream targets. The consistent involvement of Tyrosine--tRNA ligase as a mediator across these pathways suggests a possible role in the signaling cascade that ultimately leads to ATR activation. The integration of these findings highlights the kinase's potential as a downstream effector in complex metabolic or signaling networks, with Cryptobeilic Acid B serving as a key modulator in this process.",
